     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is twice the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day. The maximum is usually given as 850 mg three times daily or 1,000 mg twice daily. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual 500\u20131,000 mg per administration. A dose this high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity.\n\nWas a different dose intended? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum)\n- **1,000 mg twice daily with meals** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **1,700 mg total daily**, split into two or three doses\n\nIf 1,700 mg three times daily really is what you want, please confirm it. I can enter it with a note recording that you confirmed the dose, though I'd advise against it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
      }
     ],
